{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>et Tzipporah his daughter to Moses.</b> The reason it repeated his name and did not suffice with saying ״and he gave him et״ etc. is that the verse intends to inform us that she was his destined mate, and the word <b>to Moses</b> is the verse's own statement, saying that Tzipporah was assigned to Moses as his destined mate."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:23:38.681469856Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}